{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tr3DjhJ2DejHNhyjTBTz8p","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport Mathlib\n2\t\n3\topen Polynomial\n4\t\n5\tnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2022_b5_solution : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 (1 / 4)\n6\t/--\n7\tFor $0 \\leq p \\leq 1/2$, let $X_1,X_2,\\dots$ be independent random variables such that\n8\t$X_i=\\begin{cases}\n9\t1 & \\text{with probability $p$,} \\\\\n10\t-1 & \\text{with probability $p$,} \\\\\n11\t0 & \\text{with probability $1-2p$,}\n12\t\\end{cases}$\n13\tfor all $i \\geq 1$. Given a positive integer $n$ and integers $b,a_1,\\dots,a_n$, let $P(b,a_1,\\dots,a_n)$ denote the probability that $a_1X_1+\\dots+a_nX_n=b$. For which values of $p$ is it the case that $P(0,a_1,\\dots,a_n) \\geq P(b,a_1,\\dots,a_n)$ for all positive integers $n$ and all integers $b,a_1,\\dots,a_n$?\n14\t-/\n15\ttheorem putnam_2022_b5\n16\t(p : ℝ)\n17\t(Xset : (n : ℕ) → Set (Fin n → ℤ))\n18\t(Xprob : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → ℤ) → ℝ)\n19\t(P : (n : ℕ) → ℤ → (Fin n → ℤ) → ℝ)\n20\t(hXset : ∀ n > 0, Xset n = {X : Fin n → ℤ | ∀ i : Fin n, X i = 1 ∨ X i = -1 ∨ X i = 0})\n21\t(hXprob : ∀ n > 0, ∀ X : Fin n → ℤ, Xprob n X = ∏ i : Fin n, if (X i = 1 ∨ X i = -1) then p else (1 - 2 * p))\n22\t(hP : ∀ n > 0, ∀ (b : ℤ) (a : Fin n → ℤ), P n b a = ∑' X : {X' ∈ Xset n | (∑ i : Fin n, a i * X' i) = b}, Xprob n X)\n23\t: (0 ≤ p ∧ p ≤ 1 / 2 ∧ (∀ n > 0, ∀ (b : ℤ) (a : Fin n → ℤ), P n 0 a ≥ P n b a)) ↔ p ∈ putnam_2022_b5_solution :=\n24\tsorry\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd47984-605e-4d48-9067-78e74ef45664","uuid":"881244cd-2d4b-425d-a250-233eea4d4e7f","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:29:17.124Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/work/putnam_2022_b5.lean","content":"import Mathlib\n\nopen Polynomial\n\nnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2022_b5_solution : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 (1 / 4)\n/--\nFor $0 \\leq p \\leq 1/2$, let $X_1,X_2,\\dots$ be independent random variables such that\n$X_i=\\begin{cases}\n1 & \\text{with probability $p$,} \\\\\n-1 & \\text{with probability $p$,} \\\\\n0 & \\text{with probability $1-2p$,}\n\\end{cases}$\nfor all $i \\geq 1$. Given a positive integer $n$ and integers $b,a_1,\\dots,a_n$, let $P(b,a_1,\\dots,a_n)$ denote the probability that $a_1X_1+\\dots+a_nX_n=b$. For which values of $p$ is it the case that $P(0,a_1,\\dots,a_n) \\geq P(b,a_1,\\dots,a_n)$ for all positive integers $n$ and all integers $b,a_1,\\dots,a_n$?\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2022_b5\n(p : ℝ)\n(Xset : (n : ℕ) → Set (Fin n → ℤ))\n(Xprob : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → ℤ) → ℝ)\n(P : (n : ℕ) → ℤ → (Fin n → ℤ) → ℝ)\n(hXset : ∀ n > 0, Xset n = {X : Fin n → ℤ | ∀ i : Fin n, X i = 1 ∨ X i = -1 ∨ X i = 0})\n(hXprob : ∀ n > 0, ∀ X : Fin n → ℤ, Xprob n X = ∏ i : Fin n, if (X i = 1 ∨ X i = -1) then p else (1 - 2 * p))\n(hP : ∀ n > 0, ∀ (b : ℤ) (a : Fin n → ℤ), P n b a = ∑' X : {X' ∈ Xset n | (∑ i : Fin n, a i * X' i) = b}, Xprob n X)\n: (0 ≤ p ∧ p ≤ 1 / 2 ∧ (∀ n > 0, ∀ (b : ℤ) (a : Fin n → ℤ), P n 0 a ≥ P n b a)) ↔ p ∈ putnam_2022_b5_solution :=\nsorry\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Tr3DjhJ2DejHNhyjTBTz8p","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
